/-
Johnson/Desc/Last/ShapeDoor.lean: THE DOOR OF THE LAST CHAIN WHERE ITS PROMISE IS FILLED BY `fillZ`:
border 0's test split by the record that each of its clauses reads, and the door from three named
conditions. Definitions, statements and proofs. THE THREE CONDITIONS ARE HYPOTHESES HERE: this file
proves them only back from the door itself (`doorOwed_of_door`: from the door and start), and no
other statement of this library ends in `DoorOwed` but `doorOwed_of_less` (ShapeDoorLess.lean: from
four like conditions). WHAT OTHER FILES PROVE OF EACH. start: proved at the seated description's own
start, where the reader's second half is the record (`ProofFile.hstart_at`,
Johnson/Desc/Plain/StartThreeAtPure.lean). shared: inside the shared table's constant promise at its
last border the text `doorSharedB` holds (`Sh.last_of_on`,
Johnson/Desc/K14/Law/SharedConstLastOn.lean), and the text gives the test (`sharedDoor_of_text`,
ShapeDoorAtTexts.lean). first: reduced, not proved: the text `doorFirstB` (six of the eight tests;
of the other two: ShapeDoorLess.lean) holds inside the first table's last promise, at a record
without a mark, under `DoorStays` and `FourFacts` (`doorFirstB_of_fold`, ShapeDoorFold.lean). THE
DOOR ITSELF, the field SH₃ of `FiveF.tables_fit`: at the tower's closed value, under the head
`P5J.AtMgA`, it is proved from the computed public part, four equations on the own seats V, one
length, and `FourFacts` inside the first table's last promise, under the tower's `rc`, at a record
without a mark (`SH₃_at_free`, ShapeDoorAtFree.lean); these `FourFacts`, at o := `OnBytes.secondHashFunction`,
from four premises more (`hR_at_head`, FourAtRc.lean); ShapeDoorAtFree.lean shows neither a V that
meets its premises together nor that the head is met. AT THE HONEST THREADS, under that head at o :=
`OnBytes.secondHashFunction`: from a stand of the first thread at its last border and the start's return, the
first test (`first_door_at_end`, AtFullSide/K14/FirstDoorAtEnd.lean); from a stand of the shared
thread at its last border with its statement in order, at a p with the plan's shape of Omega, the
second (`shared_door_at_end`, AtFullSide/K14/SharedDoorAtEnd.lean), at the threads' letters, which
any value fills; that a thread stands there those files do not show.

Why. `fillZ` (Johnson/Desc/Last/ShapeRowZero.lean) lays fifteen tests into the last chain's promise
at border 0; what row 0 takes out of the promise there is owed again where the chain is entered: the
table's joint between the shared and the last chain asks, as a premise, that inside the shared
chain's last promise the start's yes gives `PL.shape 0` (`OnZero₃OfEnd₂`,
BordersLastQ.lean).
Here it is stated, and cut into what each of the two earlier chains and the description's start have
to bring. (ANOTHER DOOR: Johnson/Desc/Third/Law/AtDoor.lean speaks of the record that is handed to
the own proximity test, at border 2; this file of the chain's entry, at border 0.)

Main names (namespace `VerifiableInference.Desc.Last`).
  `firstDoorClauses h`, `firstDoorB h`: THE EIGHT TESTS THAT READ WHAT IS HANDED OF THE FIRST
    CHAIN'S LAST RECORD ALONE: its statement is tidy; its book fits; one pending row with lawful
    weights; the own group has two members; each has one sample row; the group's open rows name
    messages of the statement alone; it has an open row; a mask's number is handed.
  `sharedDoorClauses p o`, `sharedDoorB p o`: THE FIVE THAT READ THE SHARED CHAIN'S END (and the
    plan's shape of Omega) ALONE: its statement is in order; its book fits; Omega is part 0 of its
    tree; Omega is there with the plan's shape; it has one sample row.
  `start_parts`: the start's record has the statement, the own group's number and the mask's that
    were handed. **`shapeAt_zero_iff`**: `shapeAt p R 0 h o s = true` IF AND ONLY IF the start
    returns s of h and o, `firstDoorB h` and `sharedDoorB p o`: the split loses nothing and adds
    nothing. (Of the fifteen, eight and five are these; the other two, that the start returns a
    record and that the record in front is that record, are the first conjunct.)
  **`DoorOwed p fs On₂ start₃`**: the three conditions, over a letter On₂ for the shared chain's
    promise at its last border and a letter start₃ for the description's start of the last chain.
    first: inside On₂, WHERE start₃ SAYS YES, the test on what `firstOfS` takes of `fs b.1.1` says
    yes. shared: there, the test on what `sharedOfEnd` takes of K14's own end says yes. start: a yes
    of start₃ is a yes of `startAtEnds p` at `fs` and K14's end.
  **`door_fillZ`**: from `DoorOwed`: On₂ b and `start₃ b.1.1.1 b.1.1.2 b.1.2 = some s` give `(fillZ
    p R fs).shape 0 (b.1.1.1, b.1.1.2) b.1.2 s = true`: the table's premise to the letter, at On₂ :=
    its `onQ₂ …` at the last border. `doorTests_of_door`: back: where the door holds, at every b
    inside On₂ at which start₃ says yes something is handed, K14 has ended and both tests say yes.
    **`doorOwed_of_door`**: so, where the start goes as said, first and shared are the door exactly:
    no dearer.

Every "there is", walked. e (`DoorOwed.start`): tied by `ended d = some e`: at most one. f, e
(`doorTests_of_door`): tied by `firstOfS … = some f`, `ended … = some e`.
WHAT COULD GIVE THEM, BY KIND (NONE OF IT IS TYPED OR HELD HERE). first:
tidy: that each block of the first chain is a walk of quiet steps; the book: `BookFits` along the
receiving routine (Johnson/Desc/Book/BookFitsGround.lean) at each block; the two members, their
sample rows, the open row, the mask's number: the text of the first chain's last block, which lays
the own group; the names follow from tidy in kind; THE WEIGHTS: no block asks them. All must ride in
the first chain's promise (the table's letter Oc). shared: in order: walks along the shared chain;
the book; Omega's place: the shared chain's book-keeping; Omega's own shape and sample row. start:
the seating of the description's start.
Limits. (1) A REDUCTION: no condition is proved; On₂ := False makes first and shared hold emptily; a
start₃ that never says yes makes all three, and the door, hold emptily. (2) NO MEMBER: neither test
has been evaluated at a record. (3) first and shared are asked under the start's yes (without it
they are dearer than the door; the mask's laws lift nothing of them).
(4) Those of ShapeAt.lean: at plans with one answer to a sample alone; `tenantB` says yes where
Omega has no place. (5) fs is a letter. Nothing on soundness or on hiding.
Terms: lean/GLOSSARY.md.

-/
import Johnson.Desc.Last.ShapeRowZero

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

open OnBytes

namespace VerifiableInference.Desc.Last
open VerifiableInference.Desc.Third VerifiableInference.Desc.Third.Law
open VerifiableInference.Desc.Sound (bookFitsB tenantB)
open _root_.Desc.K14 (St)

/-! ## 1 Border 0's tests, split by the record that each reads -/

/-- **The tests of border 0 that read what was handed of the first chain's last record, and nothing
else**, each with its name. -/
def firstDoorClauses (h : Handed) : List (String × Bool) :=
  [("the first chain's last statement is tidy", Means.tidy4B h.st),
   ("the first chain's book fits", bookFitsB h.book),
   ("one pending row, and its row weights are lawful",
      match h.pending with
      | [r] => r.g.all (·.ok)
      | _ => false),
   ("the own group that was handed has two members",
      match h.st.groups[h.own]? with
      | some G => G.members.size == 2
      | none => false),
   ("each of the two has one sample row",
      match h.st.groups[h.own]? with
      | some G => G.members.toList.all fun i =>
          match h.st.oracles[i]? with
          | some x => x.sampleRows.size == 1
          | none => false
      | none => false),
   ("the own group's open rows name messages of the statement alone",
      match h.st.groups[h.own]? with
      | some G => G.rows.toList.all fun r => r.oracles.all fun o => decide (o < h.st.oracles.size)
      | none => false),
   ("the own group has an open row",
      match h.st.groups[h.own]? with
      | some G => !G.rows.isEmpty
      | none => false),
   ("the mask has come", h.mask.isSome)]

/-- **The tests of border 0 that read the shared chain's end (and the plan's shape of Omega), and
nothing else**, each with its name. -/
def sharedDoorClauses (p : P₁₄) (o : SharedOut) : List (String × Bool) :=
  [("the shared chain's last statement is in order", Means.inOrderB o.st),
   ("the shared chain's book fits", bookFitsB o.book),
   ("in the shared chain's book Omega is part 0 of its tree", tenantB o),
   ("Omega is there at the shared chain's end, with the plan's shape",
      match o.st.oracles[o.omega]? with
      | some y => decide (y.shape = p.S.omega)
      | none => false),
   ("Omega has one sample row at the shared chain's end",
      match o.st.oracles[o.omega]? with
      | some y => y.sampleRows.size == 1
      | none => false)]

def firstDoorB (h : Handed) : Bool := (firstDoorClauses h).all (·.2)

def sharedDoorB (p : P₁₄) (o : SharedOut) : Bool := (sharedDoorClauses p o).all (·.2)

/-- What the start's record has of what was handed. -/
theorem start_parts {p : P₁₄} {h : Handed} {o : SharedOut} {s : S₃}
    (h₀ : start₃E p.codes p.S h.st h.book h.roots h.w h.own h.mask h.pending o = .ok s) :
    s.st = h.st ∧ s.loc.own = h.own ∧ s.loc.mask = h.mask := by
  obtain ⟨f, hf, hst⟩ := start₃E_inv _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ h₀
  obtain ⟨-, -, e0⟩ := start₃_inv _ _ _ _ hst
  obtain ⟨-, e1, -, e3, e4, -⟩ := firstOutFrom_inv _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ hf
  subst e0
  exact ⟨e1, e3, e4⟩

/-- **BORDER 0's TEST IS JUST: THE START's YES, THE TEST ON THE FIRST CHAIN's END, THE TEST ON THE
SHARED CHAIN's END.** Nothing is lost and nothing is added by the split. -/
theorem shapeAt_zero_iff {p : P₁₄} {R : List Fmt.DeclaredRound} {h : Handed} {o : SharedOut} {s : S₃} :
    shapeAt p R 0 h o s = true ↔
      start₃E p.codes p.S h.st h.book h.roots h.w h.own h.mask h.pending o = .ok s ∧
        firstDoorB h = true ∧ sharedDoorB p o = true := by
  constructor
  · intro hs
    obtain ⟨s₀, h₀, ⟨hh, hm⟩, hc⟩ := shapeAt_inv hs
    simp only [clausesAt, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true, Bool.and_eq_true,
      decide_eq_true_eq] at hc
    obtain ⟨rfl, c2, c3, c4⟩ := hc
    obtain ⟨e1, e2, e3⟩ := start_parts h₀
    simp only [handedClauses, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true, Bool.and_eq_true] at hh
    simp only [memberClauses, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true, Bool.and_eq_true] at hm
    unfold namesB at c2
    rw [e1, e2] at hm c2 c3
    rw [e3] at c4
    refine ⟨h₀, ?_, ?_⟩
    · simp only [firstDoorB, firstDoorClauses, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true,
        Bool.and_eq_true]
      exact ⟨hh.1, hh.2.2.1, hh.2.2.2.2.2.2, hm.1, hm.2.1, c2, c3, c4⟩
    · simp only [sharedDoorB, sharedDoorClauses, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true,
        Bool.and_eq_true]
      exact ⟨hh.2.1, hh.2.2.2.1, hh.2.2.2.2.1, hh.2.2.2.2.2.1, hm.2.2⟩
  · rintro ⟨h₀, h1, h2⟩
    obtain ⟨e1, e2, e3⟩ := start_parts h₀
    simp only [firstDoorB, firstDoorClauses, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true,
      Bool.and_eq_true] at h1
    simp only [sharedDoorB, sharedDoorClauses, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true,
      Bool.and_eq_true] at h2
    obtain ⟨a1, a2, a3, a4, a5, a6, a7, a8⟩ := h1
    obtain ⟨b1, b2, b3, b4, b5⟩ := h2
    refine shapeAt_of h₀ ⟨?_, ?_⟩ ?_
    · simp only [handedClauses, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true, Bool.and_eq_true]
      exact ⟨a1, b1, a2, b2, b3, b4, a3⟩
    · simp only [memberClauses, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true, Bool.and_eq_true]
      rw [e1, e2]
      exact ⟨a4, a5, b5⟩
    · simp only [clausesAt, List.all_cons, List.all_nil, Bool.and_true, Bool.and_eq_true,
        decide_eq_true_eq]
      unfold namesB
      rw [e1, e2, e3]
      exact ⟨trivial, a6, a7, a8⟩

/-! ## 2 The door -/

variable {P S₁ Str : Type} (p : P₁₄) (R : List Fmt.DeclaredRound) (fs : P × S₁ → First.S)

/-- **What is owed at the door of the last chain where its promise is filled by `fillZ`**, over a
letter On₂ for the shared chain's promise at its last border and a letter start₃ for the
description's start of the last chain. -/
structure DoorOwed (On₂ : ((P × S₁) × St) × Str → Prop) (start₃ : P → S₁ → St → Option S₃) :
    Prop where
  /-- inside the shared chain's last promise, in which the first chain's rides, and where the start
  says yes: the test on what is handed of the first chain's last record says yes -/
  first : ∀ b s, On₂ b → start₃ b.1.1.1 b.1.1.2 b.1.2 = some s →
    ∀ f, firstOfS (fs b.1.1) = some f → firstDoorB f = true
  /-- there: the test on what is handed of K14's own end says yes -/
  shared : ∀ b s, On₂ b → start₃ b.1.1.1 b.1.1.2 b.1.2 = some s →
    ∀ e, _root_.Desc.K14.ended b.1.2 = some e → sharedDoorB p (sharedOfEnd e) = true
  /-- the description's start of the last chain goes by K14's end and `startAtEnds` -/
  start : ∀ pub s₁ d s, start₃ pub s₁ d = some s →
    ∃ e, _root_.Desc.K14.ended d = some e ∧ startAtEnds p pub (fs (pub, s₁)) e = .ok s

variable {p R fs}

/-- **THE DOOR AT `fillZ`**: the clause on `PL.shape 0` of `OnZero₃OfEnd₂`
(Johnson/Desc/Sound/BordersLastQ.lean), at PL := `fillZ p R fs`, from the three. -/
theorem door_fillZ {On₂ : ((P × S₁) × St) × Str → Prop} {start₃ : P → S₁ → St → Option S₃}
    (H : DoorOwed p fs On₂ start₃) (b : ((P × S₁) × St) × Str) (s : S₃) (hb : On₂ b)
    (hs : start₃ b.1.1.1 b.1.1.2 b.1.2 = some s) :
    (fillZ p R fs).shape 0 (b.1.1.1, b.1.1.2) b.1.2 s = true := by
  obtain ⟨e, he, h₀⟩ := H.start _ _ _ _ hs
  unfold startAtEnds start₃F at h₀
  cases hf : firstOfS (fs (b.1.1.1, b.1.1.2)) with
  | none =>
    rw [hf] at h₀
    cases h₀
  | some f =>
    rw [hf] at h₀
    exact fill_of_shapeAt p R _ _ hf (by rw [he]; rfl)
      (shapeAt_zero_iff.2 ⟨h₀, H.first b s hb hs f hf, H.shared b s hb hs e he⟩)

/-- **And back**: where the door holds: at every b inside On₂ at which start₃ says yes, something is
handed, K14 has ended, and both tests say yes. -/
theorem doorTests_of_door {On₂ : ((P × S₁) × St) × Str → Prop} {start₃ : P → S₁ → St → Option S₃}
    (door : ∀ (b : ((P × S₁) × St) × Str) (s : S₃), On₂ b → start₃ b.1.1.1 b.1.1.2 b.1.2 = some s →
      (fillZ p R fs).shape 0 (b.1.1.1, b.1.1.2) b.1.2 s = true)
    (b : ((P × S₁) × St) × Str) (s : S₃) (hb : On₂ b)
    (hs : start₃ b.1.1.1 b.1.1.2 b.1.2 = some s) :
    ∃ f e, firstOfS (fs (b.1.1.1, b.1.1.2)) = some f ∧ _root_.Desc.K14.ended b.1.2 = some e ∧
      firstDoorB f = true ∧ sharedDoorB p (sharedOfEnd e) = true := by
  obtain ⟨f, o, hf, ho, hz⟩ := shapeAt_of_fill p R _ _ (door b s hb hs)
  obtain ⟨e, he, rfl⟩ := Option.map_eq_some_iff.1 ho
  obtain ⟨-, h1, h2⟩ := shapeAt_zero_iff.1 hz
  exact ⟨f, e, hf, he, h1, h2⟩

/-- **So, where the start goes as said, first and shared are the door exactly.** -/
theorem doorOwed_of_door {On₂ : ((P × S₁) × St) × Str → Prop} {start₃ : P → S₁ → St → Option S₃}
    (start : ∀ pub s₁ d s, start₃ pub s₁ d = some s →
      ∃ e, _root_.Desc.K14.ended d = some e ∧ startAtEnds p pub (fs (pub, s₁)) e = .ok s)
    (door : ∀ (b : ((P × S₁) × St) × Str) (s : S₃), On₂ b → start₃ b.1.1.1 b.1.1.2 b.1.2 = some s →
      (fillZ p R fs).shape 0 (b.1.1.1, b.1.1.2) b.1.2 s = true) :
    DoorOwed p fs On₂ start₃ where
  first := fun b s hb hs f hf => by
    obtain ⟨f', _, hf', _, h1, _⟩ := doorTests_of_door door b s hb hs
    obtain rfl : f' = f := Option.some.inj (hf'.symm.trans hf)
    exact h1
  shared := fun b s hb hs e he => by
    obtain ⟨_, e', _, he', _, h2⟩ := doorTests_of_door door b s hb hs
    obtain rfl : e' = e := Option.some.inj (he'.symm.trans he)
    exact h2
  start := start

end VerifiableInference.Desc.Last

#print axioms VerifiableInference.Desc.Last.start_parts
#print axioms VerifiableInference.Desc.Last.shapeAt_zero_iff
#print axioms VerifiableInference.Desc.Last.door_fillZ
#print axioms VerifiableInference.Desc.Last.doorTests_of_door
#print axioms VerifiableInference.Desc.Last.doorOwed_of_door
